            "text": "Plugin header declares Requires PHP: 7.4 (EOL since Nov 2022) and loads files via manual require_once without composer.json, PSR-4 autoloading, or automated test configuration. — Recommendation: Add composer.json with php ^8.2|^8.3, PSR-4 autoloading, PHPUnit + PHPStan dev dependencies, and update the plugin header to Requires PHP: 8.2+. / Add defined('ABSPATH') || exit at top of file, read badge label from shortcode_atts(), and escape output with esc_html(). / Configure Composer + PHPUnit (with WP_Mock or Brain Monkey) and write unit/security regression tests covering REST permission_callback, AJAX nonces, SQL preparation, and HTML escaping. / Add declare(strict_types=1) and defined('ABSPATH') || exit to every PHP file, migrate to typed PSR-4 classes, and add complete PHPDoc annotations."
